course: dictionary
lesson: 2173
title: When things change together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A correlation is a connection between two things that change together. When one goes up or down, the other often does too. «When two things happen together, one does not have to cause the other; grown-ups say "correlation is not causation".» So two things can be linked without one making the other happen.
explain: On a scatter graph, each dot shows two numbers. If the dots rise from left to right, the two things go up together: that is a positive correlation. If the dots fall from left to right, one goes up while the other goes down: that is a negative correlation. Dots spread out with no clear pattern mean no correlation.
explain: Use the clues, just as you do with any new word. Look for words like "together", "rise", "fall" and "connection". Then ask whether one thing really causes the other, because a link on its own does not prove it.
fact: Correlation is a connection between two things that change together.
fact: "Positive correlation" means both things go up together; "negative correlation" means one goes up while the other goes down.
fact: "No correlation" means there is no clear pattern between the two things.
fact: "Correlation is not causation" means two things can be linked without one causing the other.
fact: To correlate means to go together in a pattern, and a scatter graph helps you see whether two things correlate.
exercise: «When two things happen together, one does not have to cause the other.» What does this sentence teach us? | Only numbers can be linked | Two things never happen together | *Two things can be linked without one causing the other | Every time two things happen together, one causes the other
exercise: On a scatter graph, the dots rise from left to right. What kind of correlation is this? | Negative correlation | *Positive correlation | No correlation | Sunshine correlation
exercise: Which phrase means one thing goes up while the other goes down? | Positive correlation | No correlation | Correlation is not causation | *Negative correlation
test: On a scatter graph, ice cream sales and hot days both rise together. What kind of correlation is this? | *Positive correlation | Causation | Negative correlation | No correlation
test: Two things are linked, so one must cause the other. Is this always true? | No, because correlations are always negative | Yes, if the dots are close together | Yes, a link always means a cause | *No, correlation is not causation
exam: Which phrase describes a scatter graph where the dots fall from left to right? | No correlation | *Negative correlation | Positive correlation | Strong correlation
